    [Doc][Misc] Remove redundant conjunction in RL weight transfer control flow (#19637)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    In `docs/source/user_guide/feature_guide/rl.md`, the numbered control
    flow of the
    weight transfer is written as:
    
    ```text
    4. transfer one or more groups of weights;
    5. finish the weight update; and
    6. resume generation.
    ```
    
    The fifth item ends with `; and`. The conjunction is redundant here:
    every other
    item of the list is followed by `;` alone, and the sentence already
    terminates with
    the period after the last item, so `; and` reads like a leftover from an
    `A; and B` construction that no longer exists.
    
    This PR drops the trailing `and`, leaving:
    
    ```text
    5. finish the weight update;
    ```
    
    Documentation wording only, no behavior change.
    
    Branch base: `vllm-project/vllm-ascend` `main`.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. Documentation-only wording fix, no API or runtime behavior change,
    so no
    release note fragment is needed.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Reviewed the rendered list in the feature guide page: items 1-6 now
    use the same
      `;` separator, and the period after item 6 still closes the sentence.
    - `git show --stat` shows a single one-line change in
      `docs/source/user_guide/feature_guide/rl.md`.
    - Markdown structure is untouched (no list indentation, link, or heading
    changes), so
      `markdownlint` behavior is unchanged; CI will confirm.
    - `bash format.sh ci` cannot run in this Windows environment (Schannel
    credential
      error), so the Markdown lint gate is left to CI.
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c0b6f74bee518aeaf5d72b200a0216e72fbb5e7c
    
    Signed-off-by: yangjinyang <yangjinyang5@huawei.com>

